Subject: win32u: Build without Vulkan when MoltenVK is not available

CodeWeavers' "CW HACK 25909" in vulkan_init_once() uses SONAME_LIBVULKAN
unconditionally. configure only defines it when libvulkan or MoltenVK is
found, so a build without MoltenVK fails to compile. Upstream Wine guards
the same code with #ifdef SONAME_LIBVULKAN.

Fall back to "no Vulkan" (or CX_LIBVULKAN, if set) instead.

Drop this patch once runners always build with MoltenVK, or once
CodeWeavers adds the guard.

--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c	2026-10-20 00:35:38
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c	2026-10-20 00:35:38
@@ -3006,9 +3006,19 @@
     if (!(libvulkan = getenv( "CX_LIBVULKAN" )) ||
         !(graphics_backend = getenv( "CX_ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND" )) ||
         strcmp( graphics_backend, "wined3d" ))
+#ifdef SONAME_LIBVULKAN
         libvulkan = SONAME_LIBVULKAN;
+#else
+        libvulkan = NULL;
+#endif
     else
         ERR( "Using %s\n", libvulkan );
+
+    if (!libvulkan)
+    {
+        WARN( "Vulkan support was not built in\n" );
+        return;
+    }
 
     if (!(vulkan_handle = dlopen( libvulkan, RTLD_NOW )))
     {
